Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 06-11-2026 11:15:38

Added. SSD Check: the first version, the BC250 Bazzite Suite's SSD Check on the handheld's window (owner, 06-11-2026),
written on tools/new_app.py's skeleton. A card for each drive Windows lists, with its pane: an NVMe drive's health,
power cycles, power-on hours and days, data read and written (its health log, read through Windows' storage driver
without an administrator), its firmware, NVMe version and PCIe link, the port's link when Windows reports it, the
maker's rated speeds (the BC250 app's list) and the speed measured in the handheld (X: a 1 GB test file past Windows'
cache, deleted after). A SATA drive (its SMART values need an administrator on Windows), a drive on USB and a memory
card show their specs. Y reads the drives again; RB saves a screenshot in Pictures\SSD Check and Explorer shows it. No
serial number and no firmware update check (owner, 06-11-2026).
